{"chunk_id": "4548183fcac2", "text": "After the fall of one of his chief generals, Ravana personally enters the battlefield, enraged and determined to annihilate Rama\u2019s monkey army. Vibhishana identifies the principal Rakshasa champions to Rama, highlighting the immense might and terrifying splendor of Lanka\u2019s war leaders. Ravana plunges into battle like a storm, wounding Sugriva and scattering the monkey forces. Hanuman confronts him directly and exchanges mighty blows, while Nila briefly confounds the titan king with agile tactics before being struck down. Lakshmana then duels Ravana in a fierce contest of divine weapons, but Ravana\u2019s spear pierces him and he collapses. Hanuman rescues Lakshmana and fells Ravana with a devastating strike. Finally Rama himself advances, riding Hanuman\u2019s shoulders, destroys Ravana\u2019s chariot, shatters his crown, and defeats him\u2014yet magnanimously spares his life, ordering the exhausted king to return to Lanka and come back ready for a final battle.\nRavana enters battle, defeats many monkeys and wounds Lakshmana, but Rama finally overpowers him and mercifully lets the exhausted king return to Lanka.\nThemes: heroic combat, Rama vs Ravana, divine strength, mercy in victory, loyalty of allies", "vector": [-0.005946021061390638, -0.025025341659784317, -0.003116489155218005, 0.012432589195668697, -0.012592751532793045, 0.013800641521811485, -0.015535731799900532, -0.017324209213256836, -0.028348706662654877, -0.00796806812286377, 0.01370721310377121, 0.009362814016640186, 0.006766851991415024, -0.009563016705214977, 0.005929337348788977, 0.00396735081449151, 0.04092143848538399, -0.02407771535217762, 0.021915525197982788, -0.024411385878920555, -0.005001731216907501, -0.0012587746605277061, -0.013133298605680466, -0.0056657372042536736, -0.027267610654234886, 0.014815001748502254, 0.021728668361902237, -0.02805507555603981, 0.02387751266360283, -0.00569910416379571, -0.008782226592302322, -0.01905930042266845